"""What this server exposes on the primitives a model does not drive.

MCP splits its three primitives by **who decides when one is used**: a model
chooses a tool, a host takes up a resource, a person triggers a prompt. Roles,
skills and tools reach an agent through the gateway — that is the tool
primitive, and it needs nothing declared here. This file is the other two.

Every entry names a node the tree already holds, so a capability reached this
way and reached by navigating is one capability with two addresses, never two
declarations that can drift apart.

Nothing is published on the prompt primitive to begin with. A prompt is worth
declaring only where **going wrong is expensive** — it buys consistent
execution and a guardrail, and saved typing is the weakest of the three
reasons. Declared everywhere, the menu becomes a second copy of the tool list.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

from contexture import Resource

SURFACE = (
    Resource(
        opens="$role_ref/health_runbook",
        uri="$resource_scheme://runbooks/health",
        mime_type="text/markdown",
        description="How to interpret a reachability check, and what not to conclude.",
    ),
)
